---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import '../styles/download.css';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/Hunter-124/Chudware';
---
<BaseLayout title="Get Chudware" description="Clone the public MIT source for desktop builds or browser self-hosting, or ask about optional paid hosting. Public desktop installers are not yet available.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Desktop, source, or hosting</p>
      <h1>Choose where Chudware runs.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Desktop use, source builds, and browser self-hosting have no Chudware software fee or license key. Run the prebuilt browser image, or build from the <a class="text-link" href={REPO}>public MIT source repository</a>. No public desktop installer is available yet. Optional paid, owner-operated hosting supports the project; <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">contact us about hosting</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="panel dl-primary">
        <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="download" /></span>
        <div class="dl-primary-body">
          <p class="eyebrow">Browser self-hosting · Experimental</p>
          <h2>Download and run with Docker Compose</h2>
          <p class="dl-note">From a checkout on a supported Linux host, run <code>docker compose -f web/compose.yaml up --pull always --no-build -d --wait</code> at the repository root. The public image includes the browser client and native CAD engine; no compilation or registry login is needed. The guide covers persistence and single-operator security. Online Copilot is not available in the browser.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button" href="/docs/self-hosting/">Self-hosting guide</a>
      </article>

      {/* Configured desktop packaging targets; these are not public download links. */}
      <div class="dl-grid">
        <article class="panel dl-card">
          <header class="dl-card-head">
            <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="windows" /></span>
            <h3>Windows</h3>
          </header>
          <p>Configured x86-64 packaging targets, not currently published installers:</p>
          <ul class="dl-builds">
            <li><span>Setup (.exe)</span><span>Chudware-Setup-&lt;version&gt;-x86_64.exe</span><span class="dl-build-note">For an ordinary interactive install.</span></li>
            <li><span>Installer (.msi)</span><span>Chudware-&lt;version&gt;-x86_64.msi</span><span class="dl-build-note">For managed and scripted deployment — Group Policy, Intune, msiexec.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/install-windows/">Windows setup notes <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
        </article>
        <article class="panel dl-card">
          <header class="dl-card-head">
            <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="linux" /></span>
            <h3>Linux</h3>
          </header>
          <p>Configured x86-64 release packaging targets:</p>
          <ul class="dl-builds">
            <li><span>AppImage</span><span>Chudware-&lt;version&gt;-linux-x86_64.AppImage</span></li>
            <li><span>.deb</span><span>chudware_&lt;version&gt;_amd64.deb</span></li>
            <li><span>.rpm</span><span>chudware-&lt;version&gt;-&lt;release&gt;.x86_64.rpm</span></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/install-linux/">Linux setup notes <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
        </article>
        <article class="panel dl-card">
          <header class="dl-card-head">
            <span class="dl-mark" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="apple" /></span>
            <h3>macOS</h3>
          </header>
          <p>Configured ARM64 target for Apple silicon; public packaging is not yet available.</p>
          <ul class="dl-builds">
            <li><span>App (.zip)</span><span>Chudware-&lt;version&gt;-macos-arm64.zip</span><span class="dl-build-note">Unpack a trusted build and drag Chudware into Applications.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/install-macos/">macOS setup notes <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="supporting-copy dl-sysnote">These filenames describe packaging conventions, not available downloads. Desktop builds need hardware-accelerated 3D graphics. Existing prereleases and runtime artifacts are not a public desktop installer release.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="dl-linux-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Linux packages</p>
        <h2 id="dl-linux-title">When a desktop package is available.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Use only an installer actually listed for your platform in a verified release. Distribution packages integrate with your package manager; an AppImage can run without a system install.</p>
      </header>
      <dl class="dl-formats">
        <div><dt><Icon name="package" /> .deb</dt><dd>For Debian and Ubuntu. Install with <code>sudo apt install ./chudware_&lt;version&gt;_amd64.deb</code>; removes cleanly with apt.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="package" /> .rpm</dt><dd>For Fedora, RHEL, and openSUSE. Install with <code>sudo dnf install ./chudware-&lt;version&gt;-&lt;release&gt;.x86_64.rpm</code> or zypper.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="download" /> AppImage</dt><dd>One portable file with nothing to install. Mark it executable with <code>chmod +x</code> and run it.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="dl-verify-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Verify and update</p>
        <h2 id="dl-verify-title">Check the file before you run it.</h2>
        <p class="lede">GitHub shows a SHA-256 digest beside each release asset. Compare it with <code>sha256sum</code> on Linux, <code>shasum -a 256</code> on macOS, or <code>Get-FileHash</code> in PowerShell.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="note-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">In-app updates</p>
        <p>The desktop updater requires a signed update manifest. A downloaded update must match the manifest's size and SHA-256 digest and carry a valid Ed25519 signature from the Chudware release key before the app stages it for installation. An updater does not make unpublished installers available.</p>
        <p>Use a source build you trust or an official installer after publication; do not treat a runtime-only prerelease as the desktop app.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="dl-source-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Build from source</p>
        <h2 id="dl-source-title">Free software, built on your own machine.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Chudware's MIT License permits use, modification, and redistribution; third-party components retain their own terms. The public repository README documents native build prerequisites and commands. Supported desktop SDK and native runtime dependencies are pinned release assets in this same repository, not a private companion repository.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="note-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Source code</p>
        <p>The geometry engine and UI are C++; Python provides gateway, worker, and tool services. A static WebAssembly client alone is not a complete CAD deployment: browser CAD uses the native engine on your server.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${REPO}#building-from-source`}>Native build instructions <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Optional project support</p>
      <h2>Prefer someone else to operate the server?</h2>
      <p class="lede">Ask about paid, owner-operated hosting to support development. Availability, operating terms, and data handling are discussed directly; there is no online checkout or signup. Hosting is optional, not a requirement or a software license fee.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/contact/">Ask about hosting</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/self-hosting/">Run it yourself</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
